  "notes": "USAGE:\n{安堵|あんど}する is somewhat formal and literary compared to ほっとする, which is the more colloquial equivalent. {安堵|あんど} is frequently used as a noun modifier, as in {安堵|あんど}の{表情|ひょうじょう} (expression of relief) or {安堵|あんど}{感|かん} (sense of relief).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {安堵|あんど}の{表情|ひょうじょう} (expression of relief)\n- {安堵|あんど}{感|かん} (sense of relief)\n- {安堵|あんど}の{溜|た}め{息|いき} (sigh of relief)\n- {安堵|あんど}の{色|いろ}を{浮|う}かべる (to show signs of relief)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ほっとする: to feel relieved (casual, everyday)\n- {安心|あんしん}する: to feel at ease, to be reassured",
